//! Pin for `#dt-egraph-scalar-base`
//! (`executor/model/dt_egraph_values.rs`, `AsgBuilder::gen_value`).
//!
//! Greedy-minimized from the Certora QF_UFDTLIA benchmark
//! `39657_2866defdd1f2434b69ab_47_QF_UFDTLIA.smt2` (assertions and
//! declarations pruned to the reachable set). z3 4.16.0 answers `sat`
//! instantly. The datatype `x188` is recursive with NO nullary
//! constructor; its only base constructor is scalar-only
//! (`x276 (x184 Int)`). The DT e-graph model builder generated values
//! only from zero-field constructors plus a recursive pump, so this
//! sort had no generated value at all: every free class poisoned
//! (`dt-egraph-poisoned`, 48 classes on the parent reduction), the
//! structural self-check failed, and a lane `Sat` was demoted at the
//! independent model gate to a public `unknown`. The scalar-base tier
//! renders constructors with no datatype-sorted field over canonical
//! scalar defaults, giving the pump a base. (The parent 8-assertion
//! reduction additionally trips a separate UF/DT witness-coherence
//! demotion and is not this pin.)

